   "widgets_values": [
    "## sprite-slice.json\n\nSlice a sheet into tiles (and prove the round-trip)\n\n**Does:** `SplitImageToTileList` cuts an atlas into a list of tiles - **`tile_width`/`tile_height` must match the sheet** (64x64 here, `overlap` 0) - and `SaveImage` writes one file per tile. The same tile list goes through `ImageMergeTileList` (`final_width`/`final_height` = the sheet's size) so the rebuilt sheet is saved too: if the two sheets match, the cut is exact. That round-trip is the check that `sprite-atlas.json` packs correctly.\n**Packing instead?** `sprite-atlas.json` combines individual sprites into a sheet.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S10** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E6/E33** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
